<title>SRI LANKA: Sri Lanka Agalawatte dips on profit-taking.</title>
<headline>Sri Lanka Agalawatte dips on profit-taking.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Sri Lanka's Agalawatte Plantations Ltd fell 5.88 percent or 1.50 rupees to 24 in early Tuesday trade on profit-taking, brokers said.</p>
<p>&quot;The dip is probably due to profit-taking by a small retail investor,&quot; said a broker who declined to be identified.</p>
<p>Agalawatte Plantations is one of six privatised estate firms listed on the Colombo Stock Exchange.</p>
<p>--Colombo newsroom (941) 434319</p>
